---
layout: post
title: "Seasonal flower selections for the lake tahoe bride"
date: 2026-01-15
permalink: /natures-canvas-lake-tahoe-wedding-flowers/seasonal-flower-selections-for-the-lake-tahoe-bride/
description: "From my studio to your celebration, I always encourage couples to come to a design consultation"
---

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">As a floral designer, one of my favorite parts of designing a wedding is helping couples choose flowers that feel like them and reflect the beauty of the season. In California we are fortunate to have nearly year round flower production, allowing couples to choose from an abundant selection of unique flowers. Lake Tahoe brides have an incredible range of blooms to work with: heirloom roses, wildflowers, mountain greenery, and a wide variety of hardy annuals that thrive in our climate. </p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Choosing flowers that are naturally in bloom gives your wedding an effortless sense of place. Your arrangements will feel connected to the lake, the mountains, and the time of year you are getting married. Here is a guide to the best California grown flowers available by season: </p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Spring</em> flowers are known for soft, romantic, garden-style designs. they are effortless and timeless, with movement and natural texture, and the ability to create an airy feel. Flowers of spring include <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=ranunculus" target="_blank">Ranunculus</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=anemone+flower" target="_blank">Anemones</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=tulip+la+belle+epoque" target="_blank">Tulips</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=peonies" target="_blank">Peonies</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=iris+flower" target="_blank">Iris</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=white+daffodils" target="_blank">Daffodils</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=hyacinth+flower" target="_blank">Hyacinth</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=roses" target="_blank">Roses</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=snapdragons" target="_blank">Snapdragons</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=larkspur" target="_blank">Larkspur</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=agrostemma" target="_blank">Agrostemma</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=nigella+flower" target="_blank">Nigella</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=violas+flower" target="_blank">Violas</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=queen+annes+lace" target="_blank">Queen Anne’s Lace</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=digitalis+foxglove" target="_blank">Digitalis</a> (Foxglove), <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=campanula+flower" target="_blank">Campanula</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=ammi+flower" target="_blank">Ammi</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=columbine+flower" target="_blank">Columbine</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=lupine+flower" target="_blank">Lupine</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=covenat+babies+breath" target="_blank">Heirloom Babies Breath</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=sweet+peas+flowers" target="_blank">Sweet Peas</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=poppies+flower" target="_blank">Poppies</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=saponaria+flower" target="_blank">Saponaria</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=stock+flower" target="_blank">Stock </a></p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Summer</em> flowers are vibrant and full of color. These blooms hold up well in heat and sunlight. Celosia and cosmos add interesting unique shapes and texture, while hydrangeas and dahlias bring color and fullness. Flowers of summer include <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=dahlias" target="_blank">Dahlias</a> (swoooon), <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=zinnias" target="_blank">Zinnias</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=lisianthus" target="_blank">Lisianthus</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=garden+roses" target="_blank">Garden Roses</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=hydrangea" target="_blank">Hydrangea</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=echinacea+coneflower" target="_blank">Coneflower</a> (Echinacea), <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=gladiolus" target="_blank">Gladiolus</a>. Secondary flowers: <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=celosia" target="_blank">Celosia</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=aster+flower" target="_blank">Aster</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=cosmos+flower" target="_blank">Cosmos</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=snapdragons" target="_blank">Snapdragons</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=ammi+flower" target="_blank">Ammi</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=queen+annes+lace" target="_blank">Queen Anne’s Lace</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=campanula+flower" target="_blank">Campanula</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=saponaria+flower" target="_blank">Saponaria</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=strawflower" target="_blank">Strawflower</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=yarrow+flower" target="_blank">Yarrow</a></p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Fall</em> florals are rich, warm, earthy and textured. Dahlias and mums are the main characters with their abundance of colors, shapes and textures. Flowers of fall include <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=chrysanthemums" target="_blank">Chrysanthemums</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=dahlias" target="_blank">Dahlias</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=marigolds" target="_blank">Marigolds</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=hydrangea" target="_blank">hydrangea</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=amaranth+flower" target="_blank">Amaranth</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=lisianthus" target="_blank">Lisianthus</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=roses" target="_blank">Roses</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=aster+flower" target="_blank">Aster</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=strawflower" target="_blank">Strawflower</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=celosia" target="_blank">Celosia</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=cosmos+flower" target="_blank">Cosmos</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=rudbeckia" target="_blank">Rudbeckia</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=larkspur" target="_blank">Larkspur</a></p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Winter</em> weddings have an elegant and understated beauty. Hellebores and Iceland poppies offer soft, muted color. Evergreens add structure and natural texture. Flowers of winter include <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=camellias" target="_blank">Camellias</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=hellebores" target="_blank">Hellebores</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=roses" target="_blank">Roses</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=paperwhites+flower" target="_blank">Paperwhites</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=iceland+poppies" target="_blank">Iceland Poppies</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=orchids" target="_blank">Orchids</a>, <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=evergreen+foliage" target="_blank">Evergreens </a></p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">As a Lake Tahoe wedding florist, I very much enjoy designing with California grown flowers. I find they look better because they are fresher (often harvested from the field just a few days before your event), more fragrant (few to no pesticides and sprays that eliminate the natural fragrance of flowers), and are more unique and able to create a bespoke design. Seasonal flowers also support local farms and have a less environmental footprint. </p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Industry data and reports indicate that most commercially sourced wedding flowers travel approximately 1,500 to 2,500 miles by cargo plane and vehicle from the farm where they were grown to the florist who arranges them. Flowers in our studio travel an average of 70 miles by electric vehicle. A few of our favorite local farms to support are our farm (!) <a href="https://www.thefarmgrassvalley.com" target="_blank">The Farm Grass Valley</a>, our farm neighbor <a href="https://www.sunfunnelsfield.com" target="_blank">Sunfunnels</a>, <a href="https://www.ffvines.com" target="_blank">Fresca’s Farm &amp; Vineyar</a>d, Fallen Pine Flower Farm, <a href="https://deweyfarmsflowers.com" target="_blank">Dewey Farms</a>, <a href="https://greenvalleyfloral.com" target="_blank">Green Valley Floral</a>, Sweet Mabel’s Farm. We purchase mostly from farms that offer us wholesale pricing and we are so grateful our farmers &lt;3 </p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">From my studio to your celebration, I always encourage couples to come to a design consultation with a desired vibe and color palette in mind, and let the season guide the selection. The flowers will do the rest.</p></div>
POSTEOF

echo "  [1/35] 2026-01-15-seasonal-flower-selections-for-the-lake-tahoe-bride.md"

cat > "$POSTS_DIR/2026-01-18-lake-tahoe-venues-ideal-floral-pairings.md" << 'POSTEOF'
---
layout: post
title: "Lake Tahoe venues &amp; their ideal floral pairings"
date: 2026-01-18
permalink: /natures-canvas-lake-tahoe-wedding-flowers/lake-tahoe-venues-ideal-floral-pairings/
description: "Discover perfect wedding flowers for Lake Tahoe's top wedding venues. Expert florist guide to pa"
---

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Lake Tahoe Wedding Venues and Perfect Floral Pairings </strong></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Choosing a wedding venue is one of the most important decisions you'll make, as far as wedding planning goes, and Lake Tahoe offers some of the most breathtaking locations in the world. From elegant lakeside estates to elevated mountain lodges and luxe alpine retreats, each venue has its own unique character, architecture, and natural surroundings that should guide your floral design choices.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Choosing the right florals for your Lake Tahoe wedding venue is about creating harmony between your flowers, the venue's character, and the area’s stunning natural surroundings. Each venue has its own personality, from Edgewood's refined elegance to Olympic Valley Stables' rustic charm, from The Ritz-Carlton's mountain luxury to The Chateau's European romance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The most successful Lake Tahoe wedding florals honor the venue's style while letting the natural beauty of the Sierra Nevada shine through. Whether you choose romantic garden roses, rustic wildflower arrangements, or sophisticated orchids, your flowers should feel like they belong.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>General Tips for Matching Florals to Lake Tahoe Venues</strong></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Consider Your Venue's Natural Surroundings</em></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Lake Tahoe venues come with spectacular natural backdrops, towering pines, azure waters, granite peaks, mountain meadows, or sandy beaches. Your florals should enhance, not compete with, these features. Lakeside venues benefit from florals that complement the water (blues, purples, whites,  soft colors), while mountain-forest settings pair beautifully with warmer tones and natural elements. And to tie in additional colors, think Lake Tahoe sunset colors. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Match Formality Levels</em></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">A rustic barn venue calls for different florals than a luxury resort. Ensure your floral style matches your venue's level of formality. Upscale venues like Edgewood Tahoe or The Ritz-Carlton can handle more elaborate, luxurious florals, while casual venues like Olympic Valley Stables shine with loose, organic designs.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Work With Your Venue's Color Scheme</em></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Many Lake Tahoe venues feature natural wood, stone, or specific interior colors. Visit your venue and note these permanent elements. Choose floral colors that complement rather than clash with the venue's existing palette. Rich wood tones pair beautifully with warm florals (peach, coral, burgundy), while lighter spaces can handle bolder colors.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Plan for Tahoe's Climate</em></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Lake Tahoe's high elevation, intense sun, and temperature fluctuations affect flowers differently than sea-level venues. Choose hardy blooms that can withstand these conditions. Your florist should know which flowers travel well to altitude, how to keep arrangements hydrated, and which varieties hold up in outdoor settings. On the first day of summer 2025, we got SNOW(!), and then the sun came out later in the day for the ceremony. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><em>Consider Seasonal Availability and Timing</em></p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Some Lake Tahoe venues are seasonal (only available during certain months), which naturally influences your floral options. Winter venues pair perfectly with evergreens and winter blooms, while summer-only locations can showcase the full range of seasonal flowers. Always choose flowers that are in season during your wedding month for the best quality and value.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Edgewood Tahoe Resort</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/ccb7af90-dcd4-4385-94c8-7ba3b518e3bf/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+3.53.25%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Edgewood Tahoe is the epitome of lakeside luxury. This premier resort features manicured lawns that stretch to the crystal-clear waters of Lake Tahoe, with panoramic views of the surrounding mountains. The venue offers both outdoor ceremony sites with the lake as your backdrop and elegant indoor ballroom spaces with floor-to-ceiling windows. The aesthetic is sophisticated, refined, and naturally elegant.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Edgewood </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style: Classic elegance with a touch of romance, or modern edgy.  Edgewood's refined atmosphere calls for sophisticated, timeless florals that enhance rather than overwhelm the stunning natural setting. Since the venue is luxe it can also handle a hyper modern, edgy and unique aesthetic. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Garden roses in soft whites, blush pinks, and champagne tones create romantic, luxurious bouquets and centerpieces. David Austin roses like 'Patience' and 'Juliet' offer that coveted garden-grown look with incredible fragrance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">White hydrangeas provide lush, full arrangements perfect for the ceremony altar or reception tables, echoing the pristine beauty of the lake.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Peonies (in season May-June) add a touch of romance and luxury that perfectly suits Edgewood's upscale ambiance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Delicate spray roses, ranunculus, and elegant greenery like Italian ruscus and seeded eucalyptus complete the refined aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For edgy think amaranth, and the above flowers designed in a modern way like Ikebana inspired. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Soft and sophisticated, ivory, cream, blush pink, champagne, with touches of sage green. For a bolder look, consider dusty blue to echo the lake waters, or incorporate deeper burgundy and wine tones for fall weddings.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The lake views are spectacular, so keep ceremony florals elegant but not overpowering. Low, lush centerpieces allow guests to enjoy both conversation and views. Consider a dramatic floral installation for the ballroom entrance or a statement piece near the windows to frame the lake view.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: Edgewood's natural beauty does much of the work for you. Focus your floral budget on personal flowers (bouquets, boutonnieres, corsages) and key focal points like the head table and ceremony backdrop. The venue itself provides the 'wow factor.'</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>The Ritz-Carlton, Lake Tahoe</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/9ba88fc2-7d20-4bed-9fd4-6f84dbe3568f/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+3.54.27%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Nestled mid-mountain in Northstar, The Ritz-Carlton embodies alpine luxury. This mountain estate features ski lodge elegance with soaring ceilings, grand stone fireplaces, rich wood tones, and floor-to-ceiling windows showcasing pristine forest views. The outdoor terrace offers mountain vistas, while the grand ballroom exudes sophisticated mountain elegance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for The Ritz</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Luxurious mountain romance. The Ritz calls for elevated florals that complement the rich, warm tones of the lodge while incorporating natural mountain elements.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Café au lait dahlias create stunning focal flowers that echo the warmth of the wood interiors. Their large, creamy blooms are perfect for fall weddings.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Rich burgundy and deep wine-colored roses (like Black Baccara or Burgundy) add depth and complement the lodge's warm color scheme.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Amaranth in deep burgundy adds cascading texture and a romantic, organic feel perfect for mountain weddings.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Incorporate natural elements like pine, cedar, magnolia leaves, and locally-sourced evergreen branches to bring the mountain forest indoors.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Warm and rich, deep burgundy, rust, copper, champagne, cream, with lots of greenery. For winter weddings, consider deep jewel tones (emerald, burgundy, gold) with white and evergreen accents.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The Ritz's grandeur can handle substantial floral installations. Consider tall centerpieces with dramatic branches, lush garlands along the fireplace mantels, and a show-stopping ceremony arch featuring both florals and natural wood elements. The stone and wood provide a neutral backdrop that allows for bolder floral choices.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: Take advantage of The Ritz's various spaces. Use florals to connect locations, creating a cohesive floral journey from ceremony to cocktail hour to reception. The outdoor terrace in summer is perfect for wildflower-inspired arrangements with lots of texture.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Sugar Pine Point State Park (Ehrman Mansion)</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/4cade415-a2d4-402a-ad42-fd95d19253e4/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+3.55.42%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">This historic lakeside estate features a charming 1903 mansion surrounded by towering pine trees and manicured lawns leading to a pristine beach. The venue offers a romantic, vintage feel with its historic architecture, while the natural surroundings provide a classic Tahoe mountain-meets-lake setting. Perfect for couples who appreciate history and natural beauty.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Sugar Pine Point</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Romantic vintage with garden-party charm. Think lush, overflowing arrangements that feel like they came from a turn-of-the-century garden.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Garden roses in soft, romantic colors (blush, cream, lavender) create that vintage garden aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Peonies are perfect for this venue, their old-fashioned romance matches the historic mansion perfectly.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Sweet peas, stock, and lisianthus add delicate beauty and lovely fragrance to bouquets and arrangements.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Hydrangeas in soft blues and whites echo both the lake and the vintage aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Incorporate trailing greenery like ivy and smilax for a romantic, garden-party feel.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Soft and romantic, blush pink, lavender, soft blue, cream, and white with lots of greenery. Think antique rose garden meets lakeside elegance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: This venue can handle abundant florals. Consider a lush ceremony arch, generous centerpieces with trailing elements, and a floral installation on the mansion's porch or stairs. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: The towering pines and natural landscape are already spectacular. Frame key areas with flowers rather than trying to compete with nature. A beautifully floraled ceremony space near the lake with the mansion as backdrop creates unforgettable photos.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Everline Resort &amp; Spa</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/33b4aa26-4931-4d94-84e6-52bd15d00487/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+4.01.58%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Formerly Resort at Squaw Creek, Everline Resort in Olympic Valley offers modern mountain luxury with stunning valley and peak views. The property features contemporary architecture, expansive outdoor spaces, elegant ballrooms, and a gorgeous pool terrace. The aesthetic is upscale mountain resort with a fresh, contemporary feel.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Everline</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Modern mountain elegance with refined sophistication. Everline's contemporary spaces call for clean, polished florals with both structure and natural elements.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Premium garden roses in sophisticated colors create luxurious, refined arrangements perfect for the elegant ballrooms.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Orchids (phalaenopsis or cymbidium) add contemporary elegance and exotic beauty that suits the modern aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For outdoor ceremonies, incorporate mountain elements like aspen branches, pine, and native greenery mixed with refined florals.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Calla lilies and lisianthus provide clean lines and modern elegance perfect for the contemporary spaces.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Sophisticated neutrals, white, cream, champagne, and blush. For more drama, consider blues, greens and burgundies.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The ballrooms feature modern décor that pairs beautifully with both minimalist and lush floral styles. The outdoor terrace and lawn areas offer spectacular mountain views, keep ceremony florals elegant to let the scenery shine. Consider dramatic installations in the ballroom entryway or around the dance floor.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: Everline's versatile spaces work year-round. In winter, embrace the snowy mountain views with white and evergreen arrangements. In summer, take advantage of the pool terrace for cocktail hour, floating florals in the pool create a stunning effect.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>The Chateau at Incline Village</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/644376be-96cf-4e51-8e0e-cf7bfb8f0901/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+4.00.45%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">This European-style chateau offers intimate elegance with stunning lake views. Perched in Incline Village, The Chateau features old-world charm with stone architecture, intimate spaces, and breathtaking vistas of Lake Tahoe. It's perfect for couples seeking a romantic, intimate celebration with European flair.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for The Chateau </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Romantic European elegance with luxurious details. The Chateau's intimate spaces call for lush, romantic florals with old-world charm.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Lush garden roses in rich, romantic colors, deep pinks, burgundy, champagne, and cream create that European garden aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Peonies and ranunculus add romantic, overflowing beauty perfect for the intimate spaces.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Stock and sweet peas bring old-world fragrance and delicate beauty.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Incorporate trailing elements like amaranthus, jasmine vine, or ivy for that European garden romance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Rich and romantic, deep burgundy, blush pink, champagne, cream, and ivory with lots of greenery. Gold accents add to the European luxury feel.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The intimate spaces are perfect for lush, abundant florals. Create dramatic arrangements without overwhelming the rooms, think vertical elements and cascading designs. The stone architecture provides a beautiful neutral backdrop for romantic, colorful florals.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: The Chateau's European charm pairs beautifully with candles and romantic lighting. Work with your florist to create arrangements that photograph beautifully in both natural daylight and candlelight. The lake views are stunning, so position ceremony florals to frame, not block, the vista.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Olympic Valley Stables</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/9f7c104f-45bf-4db2-bd7b-0bff20e96429/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+3.58.53%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For couples seeking rustic mountain charm, Olympic Valley Stables offers authentic barn elegance surrounded by meadows and mountain peaks. The venue features beautiful natural wood, outdoor ceremony sites with stunning valley views, and a relaxed, romantic atmosphere. This is perfect for couples who love rustic elegance and natural beauty.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Olympic Valley </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Rustic mountain romance with organic, wildflower-inspired designs. Think loose, natural arrangements that feel gathered from a mountain meadow.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wildflower-style blooms like scabiosa, yarrow, Queen Anne's lace, and nigella create that effortless meadow aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Sunflowers and zinnias add cheerful, rustic charm perfect for summer barn weddings.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Garden roses in peachy, coral, and warm tones complement the natural wood and rustic setting.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Incorporate lots of texture, wheat, dried grasses, ferns, and eucalyptus create movement and organic beauty.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Consider adding natural elements like pine cones, aspen branches, or even baby's breath for rustic romance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Warm and natural, golden yellow, burnt orange, coral, cream, and lots of greenery. For a softer look, use blush, peach, and cream with natural textures.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: Embrace the rustic setting with loose, organic arrangements. Mason jars, wooden boxes, and galvanized buckets make perfect vessels. Keep bouquets hand-tied and natural-looking. The barn's wood tones are beautiful, let them shine through rather than covering every surface.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: The meadow ceremony site is naturally gorgeous in summer. Minimal florals work beautifully, perhaps just a simple arch or two statement arrangements. Save your budget for the barn reception where florals really pop against the wood. String lights and florals create magic together in this space.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Lake Tahoe Event Center</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/2dd0f635-224d-4b4b-bdbd-8d7c76c45223/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+4.04.03%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">This versatile South Lake Tahoe venue offers a blank canvas for couples to create their dream wedding. With mountain views, flexible indoor and outdoor spaces, and modern amenities, it's perfect for couples who want complete creative control. The neutral spaces allow for any style, from modern minimalist to lavish romantic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Lake Tahoe Event Center</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Completely customizable! The blank canvas nature means florals can define your entire aesthetic. Go bold and dramatic or soft and romantic, the choice is yours.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For modern elegance: orchids, calla lilies, amaranth and structural arrangements with clean lines.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For romantic lushness: garden roses, peonies, hydrangeas in abundant, overflowing designs.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Since this is a blank slate, florals become even more important in defining your wedding's personality and style.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Completely your choice! The neutral space works with any palette. Popular choices: all white and greenery for modern elegance, jewel tones for drama,  soft pastels for romance, all blue for a lakeside wedding. </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: Since you're creating the entire aesthetic from scratch, invest in statement pieces, a dramatic ceremony arch, show-stopping centerpieces, and perhaps a floral installation as a focal point. Use florals to define different areas within the space (ceremony, cocktail, reception).</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: Work closely with your florist on the overall design concept since florals will be a major part of creating atmosphere in this space. Consider draping, lighting, and florals as a complete package. The flexibility here is amazing, you can truly create anything you envision!</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Martis Valley</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/232e69a2-0803-40d8-9767-9d9f2f1f04fb/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+4.05.49%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">This stunning private estate in Martis Valley offers breathtaking mountain meadow views, modern barn elegance, and incredible natural beauty. With expansive outdoor ceremony sites, a beautiful barn reception space, and pristine mountain surroundings, it's ideal for couples seeking upscale rustic elegance in a spectacular setting.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Martis Valley</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Elevated rustic elegance with natural sophistication. Think refined barn wedding with high-end touches and abundant natural beauty.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Garden roses in sophisticated colors (champagne, blush, peach) create refined romance perfect for upscale barn elegance.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Dahlias in warm tones add visual impact and complement the mountain meadow setting beautifully.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Mix in wildflower-inspired elements like scabiosa, astilbe, and delphinium for that mountain meadow connection.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Incorporate natural textures, wheat, grasses, ferns, and abundant greenery create organic sophistication.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Warm sophisticated neutrals, champagne, blush, peach, cream, and sage green. For fall, add rust, burnt orange, and deep burgundy.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The outdoor ceremony site with mountain views is spectacular, keep florals beautiful but not overpowering so the natural scenery remains the star. Inside the barn, go more dramatic with lush centerpieces and installations. The modern barn aesthetic pairs beautifully with both rustic and elegant florals.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: The natural meadow setting in summer is unbeatable. If you're marrying in peak wildflower season (July-August), let the surrounding meadows inspire your palette. The barn's clean lines and neutral tones mean florals really pop, this is a great venue for making a statement with your floral design.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Old Greenwood, Truckee</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/5392dc5a-78a1-4b94-a033-8409ae229d87/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+4.07.23%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Old Greenwood's clubhouse offers classic mountain elegance with stunning Tahoe views. The venue features beautiful stone and timber architecture, expansive windows, mountain vistas, and both indoor and outdoor ceremony options. It's sophisticated mountain lodge meets country club elegance, perfect for refined mountain celebrations.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for Old Greenwood</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Classic mountain elegance with refined sophistication. Old Greenwood calls for polished, timeless florals that complement the upscale mountain setting.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Premium roses in classic colors (white, cream, blush) create timeless elegance perfect for the refined setting.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Hydrangeas provide lush, full arrangements that photograph beautifully and suit the upscale aesthetic.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For fall weddings, incorporate dahlias and garden roses in warm tones that echo the mountain setting.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add mountain elements like pine, cedar, and eucalyptus to ground the arrangements in the Tahoe setting.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Classic and sophisticated, ivory, cream, champagne, and blush with touches of greenery. For more drama, consider burgundy and cream or navy and blush combinations.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The clubhouse's elegant architecture and mountain views create a refined backdrop. Use florals to enhance without overwhelming, think classic, well-designed arrangements rather than overly trendy styles. The outdoor terrace ceremony site has beautiful views, so keep florals elegant and frame the vista.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: Old Greenwood's neutral palette and classic architecture work beautifully with timeless floral designs that will look stunning in photos for years to come. The stone and wood tones are warm, so lean into warmer floral colors rather than cool tones for the most harmonious look.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;"><strong>Hyatt Regency Lake Tahoe Resort</strong></p></div>


  
      <img src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/67e81d7599b7ef0dec0ec81c/258d4bb5-917a-49db-bda9-a8d7471710cf/Screenshot+2026-02-07+at+4.10.01%E2%80%AFPM.png?format=original" alt=""/>
  

<div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The Hyatt Regency in Incline Village offers sophisticated lakeside elegance with multiple ceremony and reception options. From the Lone Eagle Grille's stunning lakeside setting to the Grand Ballroom's mountain-modern aesthetic, this venue provides upscale versatility. The property balances contemporary luxury with natural beauty.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Floral Pairings for The Hyatt</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Style Direction: Sophisticated elegance with contemporary touches. The Hyatt's refined aesthetic calls for polished, upscale florals with clean lines and thoughtful design.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Recommended Flowers: </p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Premium garden roses in elegant colors create luxurious, sophisticated arrangements.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Orchids (phalaenopsis or cymbidium) add exotic elegance and contemporary flair.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Calla lilies provide clean, modern lines that complement the contemporary spaces.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Lisianthus adds delicate beauty with a more refined aesthetic than traditional roses.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Incorporate elegant greenery like Italian ruscus, salal, and eucalyptus for polish and texture.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Color Palette: Refined neutrals, white, cream, champagne, and blush with touches of gold or silver. For more drama, consider navy and white, or deep plum with blush and cream.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Design Tips: The Grand Ballroom can handle substantial centerpieces and dramatic installations. Consider tall centerpieces on some tables with low arrangements on others for visual variety. Lighting is key in the ballroom, work with your florist to ensure flowers photograph beautifully under both natural and artificial light.</p><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Florist Insider Tip: If you're getting married at the Lone Eagle Grille, the lakeside location is absolutely stunning, minimal florals are needed for the ceremony. The indoor spaces are sophisticated and can handle elegant, upscale floral designs. The Hyatt team is experienced with large weddings, making logistics smooth for your florist.</p></div>
POSTEOF

